course: dictionary
lesson: 8707
title: Send and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Send usually means to make something go to another place or person, like a letter or a message. «A landline phone sends the call along a wire or fibre to an exchange and on to the other phone.» Here send means the call travels from one phone to another.
explain: Send can also mean to tell someone to go somewhere. «The referee's word is final: a red card sends a player off.» The player is told to leave the game. Send can also mean to make something move fast, or to ask someone to come. Check the sentence: which meaning fits best?
explain: Send is a verb, so its forms change with time: send, sends, sent, sending. Today I send, yesterday I sent. «Messages can be saved, shared and misunderstood, so you never send what you would not say face to face.» This sentence is about messages you type, and it gives a safety rule: think before you send.
fact: Send means to make something go to another place or person.
fact: To send someone is to tell them to go somewhere, as in «a red card sends a player off».
fact: To send something flying means to make it move very fast.
fact: To send for someone means to ask them to come.
fact: Never send photos or your address to strangers online.
exercise: Sam says, «I will send you a text after the match.» What does send mean here? | To make something fly very fast | To tell someone to go home | *To make a message go to another person | To ask someone to come
exercise: «A red card sends a player off.» What does sends off mean? | To ask the player to come back | To make the player run very fast | *To tell the player to leave the game | To give the player a present
exercise: Which word is the past tense of send? | sends | *sent | sender | sending
test: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears, which may help cubs follow their mother and send signals.» What does send mean in this sentence? | To ask for help | *To pass signals to others | To run away fast | To tell them to go home
test: What is the safest thing to do online? | Send your address to a stranger | *Think before you send, and never share your address with strangers | Send everything you write without reading it first | Send a photo to anyone who asks
exam: Mum says, «Please send Ella to bed now.» What does send mean? | To make Ella run fast | To post a letter to Ella | To ask Ella to come here | *To tell Ella to go to bed
